/**
 * @module
 * Type checking (design/compiler-architecture.md 6; stage 0:
 * bootstrap/src/sema/check.c and check_internal.h): signatures first, then
 * constants and function bodies, one function at a time. Expressions are
 * checked bidirectionally: `checkExpr` receives the type the context
 * expects (`ERROR` when there is none) as a hint and gives the type it
 * finds, kept by `NodeId`; `coerce` then reports a mismatch. Divergence is
 * a type: `return`, `break` and infinite loops have type `!`.
 *
 * The bodies of std functions are checked only when a program uses them
 * (stage 0 checks them when the lowering reaches them): stage 1 checks
 * those of the root module, and of every module outside std.
 */

